{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWXrXvW3TyVJNwLLeLWj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QsdemdDmjgxKjKs49dgmBh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md","content":"# CVE Blast Radius Analysis: axios ReDoS (CVE-2021-3749)\n\n## 1. CVE Identification\n\n- **CVE:** CVE-2021-3749\n- **Affected package:** `axios` (npm)\n- **Vulnerability type:** Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS)\n- **Root cause:** `trim()` in `/workspace/axios/lib/utils.js:189-190` uses two catastrophically-backtracking regexes:\n  ```js\n  function trim(str) {\n    return str.replace(/^\\s*/, '').replace(/\\s*$/, '');\n  }\n  ```\n- **Exploit path:** `/workspace/axios/lib/helpers/parseHeaders.js:37-38` calls `utils.trim()` on every line of every HTTP response header while parsing responses (`key = utils.trim(line.substr(0, i))`, `val = utils.trim(line.substr(i + 1))`). A malicious or compromised server (or a MITM) can return a crafted header value that causes catastrophic backtracking in the `trim` regex, blocking the Node.js event loop / browser main thread.\n- **Affected version range:** `< 0.21.2`\n- **Fixed in:** `0.21.2` (patch replaced the regex-based trim with `String.prototype.trim()`)\n\n## 2. Direct Dependents\n\n| Repo | Manifest | Declared axios range | Local path |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| axios (the vulnerable package itself) | `/workspace/axios/package.json` | `0.21.1` (self) | `/workspace/axios/package.json` |\n| grafana | `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/package.json` | `^0.26.1` | `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/package.json:73` |\n| druid | `/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json` | `^0.26.1` | `/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json:71` |\n\nNo other `package.json` in either the `grafana` or `druid` workspace declares `axios` as a direct dependency. The Grafana root `package.json` (`/workspace/grafana/package.json`) does **not** depend on axios at all — Grafana's core frontend uses its own `backendSrv`/`fetch`-based HTTP client, not axios.\n\n## 3. Transitive Paths\n\n### Grafana\n- Root `package.json` (`/workspace/grafana/package.json`) defines a Yarn workspace (`workspaces.packages: [\"packages/*\", \"plugins-bundled/internal/*\"]`) — axios is **not** hoisted from any of the core app's `dependencies`/`devDependencies`.\n- The only path into the tree is `@grafana/toolkit` (`/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/package.json`), a **build/CLI tool** used by plugin developers to scaffold, build, sign, and publish Grafana plugins — it is a devDependency of the root workspace (`\"@grafana/toolkit\": \"workspace:*\"` in `/workspace/grafana/package.json:107`), not something shipped inside Grafana itself or inside any bundled plugin's runtime bundle.\n- Actual axios usage inside grafana-toolkit:\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/cli/tasks/plugin.ci.ts:247-248` — `require('axios')` to POST CI reports to an external endpoint.\n  - `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/src/cli/utils/githubRelease.ts:1,76,80` — imports `AxiosResponse` and uses an axios-based GitHub client to create/delete plugin releases.\n- The single bundled internal plugin (`/workspace/grafana/plugins-bundled/internal/input-datasource/`) has no axios dependency.\n- No evidence of a \"plugin SDK vendoring axios\" — `@grafana/data`, `@grafana/runtime`, `@grafana/ui`, `@grafana/e2e`, `@grafana/e2e-selectors`, and `@grafana/schema` package.json files contain no axios reference.\n\n### Druid\n- `/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json:71` declares `axios: ^0.26.1` directly.\n- axios is a **core, actively-used runtime dependency** of the web console frontend (not a build tool), imported directly in numerous source files, e.g.:\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/singletons/api.ts:19-29` — the shared `Api` singleton wraps `axios.create()` for all console→Druid-cluster API calls.\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/utils/query-manager.tsx:19-129` — uses `axios.CancelToken`/`axios.isCancel` for query cancellation.\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/utils/druid-query.ts:19-302` — issues SQL queries via axios and inspects `AxiosResponse`/`axios.isCancel`.\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/helpers/execution/sql-task-execution.ts:19-188` — task/report polling via `AxiosResponse`.\n  - `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/views/workbench-view/{helper-query,query-tab}/*.tsx` and `/workspace/druid/web-console/src/views/sql-data-loader-view/schema-step/rollup-analysis-pane/rollup-analysis-pane.tsx` — additional UI call sites.\n  - This means every response the Druid web console receives from a Druid cluster is parsed via axios's header-parsing path.\n- `/workspace/druid/licenses.yaml:5407-5414` independently confirms the resolved license/version metadata for the `web-console` module: `name: axios`, `version: 0.26.1`, `module: web-console` — corroborating the manifest-declared range with the actual resolved/bundled version.\n\n## 4. Version Analysis — Are We Vulnerable?\n\n| Repo | Resolved axios version | Vulnerable to CVE-2021-3749 (`< 0.21.2`)? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/axios` (upstream package under evaluation) | `0.21.1` (`/workspace/axios/package.json:3`) | **Yes** — squarely inside the vulnerable range. This is the version whose code was inspected above and confirmed to contain the unpatched `trim()` regex. |\n| `/workspace/grafana` (`@grafana/toolkit`) | `^0.26.1` declared; no lockfile-pinned axios entry was found elsewhere in the workspace (axios is not hoisted into any other package) | **No** — `0.26.1` is well past the `0.21.2` fix boundary. |\n| `/workspace/druid` (`web-console`) | `0.26.1` resolved (confirmed via `/workspace/druid/licenses.yaml:5413`, matching the `^0.26.1` range in `/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json:71`) | **No** — patched version already in use. |\n\n**Bottom line:** The vulnerable `0.21.1` axios code exists only in the `axios` repository itself (the library under CVE analysis). Neither of the two real consuming projects in this workspace — Grafana (via `@grafana/toolkit`, a plugin-dev CLI tool) nor the Druid web console (a core runtime dependency) — is actually exposed: both have already moved to `0.26.1`, which is patched. There is no evidence of a vendored/duplicate copy of the vulnerable `0.21.1` axios anywhere under `/workspace/grafana` or `/workspace/druid`.\n\n## Summary / Prioritization\n\n- **No active exploitability found** in `grafana` or `druid` for CVE-2021-3749 — both already consume a patched axios (`0.26.1`).\n- If the `/workspace/axios` checkout at `0.21.1` is itself published/consumed anywhere outside this workspace (e.g., an internal mirror, a pinned lockfile elsewhere, or a Grafana/Druid plugin not present in this repo snapshot), that would be the actual remaining risk surface — recommend auditing any external plugin repos or internal registries that might still resolve to `axios@0.21.1` (or any `<0.21.2` version) via lockfile pins or `resolutions` overrides not present in these two workspaces.\n- Recommended action: no patch required for `grafana` or `druid` based on current manifests/resolved versions; treat this as closed for these two repos, and use the confirmed vulnerable code path (`/workspace/axios/lib/utils.js:189-190` via `/workspace/axios/lib/helpers/parseHeaders.js:37-38`) as the detection signature if scanning other repos.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9ac8a-b099-45b2-93e4-2aa22b90cd3a","uuid":"08b83029-44d5-438f-8e70-bae91b1e9db8","timestamp":"2026-07-29T14:48:49.944Z","request_id":"req_011CdWXrWBaajQDttP21ugjC"}
